<%#
  Swapped in for whatever container the write action already knew about
  (composer_<block_id>, thread_<node_id>, comment_<node_id>) when the
  underlying resource is gone or no longer visible to the viewer
  (Github::NotFound / Github::Forbidden) — reloading the page will hit
  D's own GithubErrorHandling and show the full explanation; this just says
  enough to explain why nothing happened.

  It borrows the composer's own card so the explanation lands in the shape of
  the thing that was about to be there.

  Locals: message: (required) String
%>
<div class="composer-card mt-3" data-testid="inline-error" role="alert">
  <p class="composer-note composer-note--error pb-2.5"><%= local_assigns.fetch(:message) %></p>
</div>
